PROTOCOL REFERENCES (specifications, not code)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* "WireGuard: Next Generation Kernel Network Tunnel" - Jason A. Donenfeld (protocol specification)
* RFC 7693  - The BLAKE2 Cryptographic Hash and Message Authentication Code
* RFC 7748  - Elliptic Curves for Security (X25519)
* RFC 8439  - ChaCha20 and Poly1305 for IETF Protocols
* RFC 6479  - IPsec Anti-Replay Algorithm without Bit Shifting
No code is copied from the Linux kernel's GPL-2.0 `wireguard.ko` module, from `wireguard-tools`,
or from any other GPL-licensed VPN implementation. Those tools are used only inside the test
harness (as separate processes) to prove interoperability, which does not create a derivative work.

